{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers","id":380970,"title":"Changing Moon Lunar Caste Anima Powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-25T07:47:31-08:00","id":380970,"title":"Changing Moon Lunar Caste Anima Powers","content":"In 3rd Edition, Lunars can control how others perceive them, but they cannot construct phantasmal illusions of sight and sound. For assuming the appearances of specific other individuals, they need to use Heart's Blood to guide their shapeshifting, or perhaps use a shapshifting Charm to assist a mundane Larceny disguise roll.<br /> <br /> So the first anima effect of the Changing Moon Caste doesn't fit, anymore. If it ever did.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the first place, it seems to have been created in First Edition along the line of thought that the Changing Moon Caste should be the best Lunars at &quot;shapeshifting&quot;. Back in the days of tangled, cross-Attribute Charm trees, every single Charm that altered the Lunar's form or the form of anything else was arbitrarily based on a <i>Social Attribute</i> for that very reason.<br /> <br /> It was so bad that, in a reflection of the Twilight-as-Dawn-Caste problem, people who wanted to play Lunars to enjoy actually being a shapeshifting demigod would shoehorn every character concept into being a Changing Moon when otherwise it should have been a Full Moon or No Moon.<br /> <br /> The first anima effect was a patch on the difficulties of Heart's Blood theft in the days when no writer seemed to consider alternative (and non-lethal) methods for stealing Heart's Blood. It also furthered the character-concept problem created by the Socially Attributed shapeshifting Charms, in making the Changing Moons the one Caste that could freely touch on the &quot;use other people's faces&quot; shapeshifter archetype.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second Edition started to give us other methods for acquiring Heart's Blood that didn't necessarily require leaving an incriminating trail of corpses and disappearances, but it was too stingy or too late (or both) with those methods. The Charm trees were now broken into single-Attribute paths and shapeshifting (internal or external) could be found in Physical and Mental Charms. The Changing Moons were no longer &quot;the most Lunar of Lunars&quot;, because now everyone was free to be the shapeshifter they were meant to be, with their Caste merely determining what kind of Lunar they were best at being.<br /> <br /> Except these changes weren't reflected in the anima banners at all. Full Moons kept their effects (which largely worked to begin with), No Moons kept their sorcery-effect (broadened into a general Occult-based thing that really didn't help with anything besides Sorcery), and Changing Moons still kept their old effect, but poorly translated into Second Edition's mechnical system. There were upgrades and attempted patches, but overall it was a copy-paste without apparent consideration for how well those fit the Castes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Changing Moons are the socially inclined Lunars. They favor Charisma, Manipulation and Appearance. The Charms they favor most make them terrifying, persuasive, beautiful, larger than life.<br /> <br /> In First Edition, you could gain Heart's Blood just by being the one to inflict the last fatal blow to a creature. A Full Moon would fight and kill a beast directly with his great strength. A No Moon would learn its habits and diet, and prepare a trap with poisoned food and spiked pits. But a Changing Moon would use his social affluence to hire a group of professional hunters to bring the beast down and let him have the final killing shot.<br /> <br /> Should the Changing Moon Caste anima effects double down on the disguising abilities that a Changing Moon already possesses as a Lunar Exalted with the power of Heart's Blood shapeshifting and Social Attribute Charms? Or should their anima effects instead emphasize the fact that they are the Caste of Lunars who most often use persuasion, intimidation and seduction to achieve their ends, whether in stolen forms or their very own?<br /> <br /> I'm happy with the Full Moon anima abilites, as those definitely emphasize the fact that the Full Moons are the Lunars who most often use physical power and speed to achieve their goals, no matter what forms they use. Full Moons did not (and should not) get anima effects which compete with their existing native shapeshifting powers to provide another War Form or source of giant, strong animal shapes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-26-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:55:40-08:00","id":381323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers#post380970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They favor Charisma, Manipulation and Appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this is part of the problem, and I hope that he same thing is done with Lunars as with Solars - picking Favoreds from a bigger list, rather than having a default 5. Simply because Changing Moons are the only Lunar Caste with two potentially-redundant Attributes as Caste. Cha and Man can overlap quite a bit in non-Charm application, something that you can't say for anything in the Full or No Moon spreads (No Moons have their own problem with their anima, but that's another issue). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers#post380970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should the Changing Moon Caste anima effects double down on the disguising abilities that a Changing Moon already possesses as a Lunar Exalted with the power of Heart's Blood shapeshifting and Social Attribute Charms? Or should their anima effects instead emphasize the fact that they are the Caste of Lunars who most use persuasion, intimidation and seduction to achieve their ends, whether in stolen forms or their very own?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good question. I am inclined to say that Changing Moons being more equivalent to the Solar Night in terms of infiltration skills, but approached through a different lens, is not inherently a bad thing. In the end I'm not sure the distinction you're making is quite as big as you think it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:45:34-08:00","id":381562,"title":"","content":"The Changing Moon anima always seemed mechanically awkward to me, and I think you summed it up pretty well. I changed lots of things in my games, but never tried tackling that one, since I never had a player who wanted to play a Changing Moon. Definitely was never a fan though, and if it got changed I wouldn't shed any tears. <br /> <br /> Do you have any ideas for what you would like to see replace it Sunder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T21:17:34-08:00","id":381570,"title":"","content":"I keep on trying to think of what Anima Style power I would give them that doesn't feel like it infringes on what should just be generally available lunar charms. Honestly I kinda like the fact that they are Mystique style shapeshifters, and I think I would be ok with Changing Moons being the only Lunars who specialize in human transformations without taking hearts-blood.<br /> <br /> I think you make a good point in trying to tie their anima back into their social focus, but I also think the current Lunar animas work really well as a reflection of their broken and re-formed castes. The Lunars were hunted and harried for many centuries and their new animas reflect that, you have the Full Moons who survived by being the terribly strong and fast monsters in the wilds, the Changing Moons who danced from face to face until they slipped their pursuers, and the No Moons who perfected shadowy magicks to conceal themselves and warn them of danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T21:54:17-08:00","id":381609,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking a bit about the logic of Anima powers lately. Unfortunately, I don't feel I can give an answer to the topic's question, but there may be some food for thought in my mild ramblings about where they come from.<br /> <br /> Anima powers flow from and otherwise especially suit a given Caste, what that Caste is meant to be, and what it is meant to do (and how). They are capabilities that should be exclusive to members of that Caste out of all in the splat, are things that members of the Caste shouldn't have to pay for, and/or abilities that don't feel like they'd work especially well as Charms for one reason or another. Eclipses are meant to be diplomats, walkers-in-all-courts, and facilitators of harmonious agreements. Toward these ends, they get otherworldly diplomatic immunity, they may learn the ways of those in such courts, and agreements they sanction bring wrath on the heads of individuals who break them.<br /> <br /> So, before I'd feel comfortable answering the question of whether it's an appropriate power -- or what appropriate powers might take its place -- I feel I'd need a better understanding and definition of what exactly the Caste is meant to be and do, particularly in the context of EX3 Lunars. Which... I feel woefully ill-equipped to know, at this point. :/ So, apologies for the mildly long-winded path toward, &quot;I dunno.&quot;<br /> <br /> The following is a point I meandered off into that I don't feel is quite pertinent, and may in fact be glaringly obvious when I see it tomorrow morning. Just in case it's not, I'll leave it in. To the ends of helping people ignore it, I'll drop it into a spoiler box. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Another note is that the Anima powers of some other splats' Castes/Aspects tend to have a certain &quot;theme&quot; to them. Solar Caste Anima powers grant them the capabilities to best fulfill the heroic roles for which the Unconquered Sun Chose them. Terrestrial Aspect Anima powers grant some of the untamed fury of an element and reflect the blood-born connections and empathy with them. Sidereal Caste Anima powers grant the knowledge to weave a secret sign by which they may grace their actions -- and more notably, all nearby allies -- with the blessing of a Maiden. Should Lunars have such an Anima &quot;theme?&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T22:22:41-08:00","id":381614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381609#post381609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another note is that the Anima powers of some other splats' Castes/Aspects tend to have a certain &quot;theme&quot; to them. Solar Caste Anima powers grant them the capabilities to best fulfill the heroic roles for which the Unconquered Sun Chose them. Terrestrial Aspect Anima powers grant some of the untamed fury of an element and reflect the blood-born connections and empathy with them. Sidereal Caste Anima powers grant the knowledge to weave a secret sign by which they may grace their actions -- and more notably, all nearby allies -- with the blessing of a Maiden. Should Lunars have such an Anima &quot;theme?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree that Animas should represent the very core concept of a Caste or Aspect, and perhaps even assure that an exalt of a certain Caste will be better at that role than any other exalt who puts a equal amount of effort into filling it without the Anima. I also agree that the Changing Moons may need a better defined role before you can start to consider what their Anima should be. Full Moons are the Big Bad Wolves the terror of nature incarnate, No Moons are the Baba Yagas wielding weirdness and shamanistic power, but I'm not sure who the Changing Moons are?<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to say they are Nanabozho/Nanabush the Ojibwa hero, both a trickster and a guide. He could be deceitful and wild, but these were just means to an end of teaching important lessons and bringing an order to the world. One of Nanabozho's greatest powers was transformation, something very much in line with Lunars in general, but I think this could be tweaked a little to specifically be taking human forms. Nanabozho took animal forms because the Ojibwa morality plays were told through the lens of animal creation myths, in Exalted the moral myths of Changing Moons could instead be told through the lens of the many-faced guide who arrived to set an order to the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 01-26-2015, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T05:47:28-08:00","id":381812,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that for Ex3, Solars are getting multiple anima powers - the same is likely to be true of Abyssals, and who's to say it won't also carry over for Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Getimians...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:25:58-08:00","id":381949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381812#post381812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that for Ex3, Solars are getting multiple anima powers - the same is likely to be true of Abyssals, and who's to say it won't also carry over for Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Getimians...?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact Dragonblooded have had multiple abilities on their animas for a while now. Air aspects slow fall, jump high and ger DV bonuses, wood aspects get DV and natural poison and poison immunity, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:37:33-08:00","id":381963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381562#post381562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any ideas for what you would like to see replace it Sunder?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381570#post381570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep on trying to think of what Anima Style power I would give them that doesn't feel like it infringes on what should just be generally available lunar charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like TurkeyGiant says, you kind of want to give them something that doesn't feel like it infringes on Charms.<br /> <br /> Still, the Full Moon anima effects manage to enhance what you could learn to do with Charms without a problem. Since that's the best Lunar anima for two Editions, let's actually try using that for a model.<br /> <br /> <br /> Full Moons double their running and leaping distance in both editions, and since Journeys Caste Sidereals could do that and more, Second Edition added the power to double the Lunar's Strength rating for the purposes of Feats of Strength.<br /> <br /> So maybe a Changing Moon could add her Essence rating to her Charisma or Manipulation for the purposes of Intimidation actions, and to her Appearance for seduction actions. In much the same way that Earth Aspects can add their Essence to their Soak.<br /> <br /> No Moons would get to add their Essence in dice to any action using an Ability from the &quot;Wisdom&quot; list on their character sheet (Bureaucracy, Craft, Investigation, Medicine, Lore, Occult)? I dunno.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381570#post381570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I kinda like the fact that they are Mystique style shapeshifters</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have explicitly stated that Lunars are not Mystique. You can check the What We Know wiki for more details on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you make a good point in trying to tie their anima back into their social focus, but I also think the current Lunar animas work really well as a reflection of their broken and re-formed castes. The Lunars were hunted and harried for many centuries and their new animas reflect that, you have the Full Moons who survived by being the terribly strong and fast monsters in the wilds, the Changing Moons who danced from face to face until they slipped their pursuers, and the No Moons who perfected shadowy magicks to conceal themselves and warn them of danger. </div> </div> </div>While you have a point, the fact is that ANY and ALL Lunars can and should be able to &quot;dance from face to face&quot; to escape pursuit. That's Heart's Blood, not Charms. To the extent that turning into humans requires a Charm or Knack, it should only be just one entry-level purchase, as it was in Second Edition. (First Edition doesn't bear mentioning, because everything had ridiculously long prerequisite chains.)<br /> <br /> If the Full Moon anima is about surviving based on strength, then the Changing Moon anima can be about surviving based on the powers of intimidation and seduction. It should not be about doubling down on an effect on one's &quot;Lunar-ness&quot;, because what does that say about the other Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-26-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:52:46-08:00","id":382140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381963#post381963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs have explicitly stated that Lunars are not Mystique. You can check the What We Know wiki for more details on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But could ONE of the castes have that sort of power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381963#post381963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you have a point, the fact is that ANY and ALL Lunars can and should be able to &quot;dance from face to face&quot; to escape pursuit. That's Heart's Blood, not Charms. To the extent that turning into humans requires a Charm or Knack, it should only be just one entry-level purchase, as it was in Second Edition. (First Edition doesn't bear mentioning, because everything had ridiculously long prerequisite chains.)<br /> <br /> If the Full Moon anima is about surviving based on strength, then the Changing Moon anima can be about surviving based on the powers of intimidation and seduction. It should not be about doubling down on an effect on one's &quot;Lunar-ness&quot;, because what does that say about the other Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest though that the free form face-dancing could be the sole purview of the Changing-Moons, where other Lunars need heart's blood, they can imitate or create whatever face they need (when I say face I specifically mean people not animals). This would be an awesome power but it would also have its limits, I would rule that Changing Moon face-dancing could not be paired with other charms that require you to have heart's blood to take the form, that way you couldn't use charms to supernaturally steal the intimacies, skills, and powers of a you person were only superficially appearing as with the Changing-Moon anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T11:02:07-08:00","id":382146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381963#post381963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs have explicitly stated that Lunars are not Mystique. You can check the What We Know wiki for more details on that.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I don't think Mystique is the best Lunar inspiration. I saw her quite a bit but never knew much about her. From what I saw, she was a conniving coward and a psychologically abusive mother. If shapeshifting is all it takes to make you a Lunar, so is the T-1000 and that guy from Deep Space Nine.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also went back and looked at John's quote on Mystique, his point seems to be that she personally doesn't act very Lunar like, and shape-shifting alone isn't enough to make a Lunar. But I don't think either of those comments preclude Changing-Moons from having a anima power similar to her mutant power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:42:10-08:00","id":382394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=381949#post381949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact Dragonblooded have had multiple abilities on their animas for a while now. Air aspects slow fall, jump high and ger DV bonuses, wood aspects get DV and natural poison and poison immunity, ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call those &quot;multiple anima powers,&quot; for the most part, more just &quot;deriving multiple kinds of benefit from the same one power.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:52:30-08:00","id":382401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=382146#post382146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also went back and looked at John's quote on Mystique, his point seems to be that she personally doesn't act very Lunar like, and shape-shifting alone isn't enough to make a Lunar. But I don't think either of those comments preclude Changing-Moons from having a anima power similar to her mutant power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, though. Mystique is a shapeshifter. Odo is a shapeshifter. T-1000 is a shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> What we've had for Lunars from the very beginning is that they're shapeshifters. So it's natural to think of these examples as being Lunar in theme.<br /> <br /> Except now, Lunar themes are more than just shapeshifting. So these examples aren't very applicable. The problem is, we don't know what their main theme really is going to be at this point, so it's hard to guess at what mythic an pop culture references are truly in theme for 3e Lunars.<br /> <br /> That said, that kind of face-dancing might well work for the Changing Moons in particular where it's not really representative of how all Lunars work, or what all Lunars' themes are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T16:34:36-08:00","id":382429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers?p=382401#post382401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, that kind of face-dancing might well work for the Changing Moons in particular where it's not really representative of how all Lunars work, or what all Lunars' themes are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social Anima powers are probably the hardest to figure out if you want to do more than just give a straight up bonus. I figure the face-dancing works as an &quot;outside the box&quot; power that is 50/50, utility and social focused. The No-Moons have a bit of that same problem, I think their plain potency in the occult is pretty good, but maybe they also could get access to some specifically No-Moon Anima powered equivalent to thaumaturgy or sorcery, call it Black Moon Rites or something? Not on the same scale as Sorcery, just a small series of Lunar rites and rituals.<br /> <br /> Who is responsible for giving the moon-silver tattoos, I would assume it's often No-Moons. Maybe their application could be folded into the Black Moon Rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 01-26-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T22:27:48-08:00","id":382754,"title":"","content":"I just lost an entire post due to a sudden and inexplicable webbrowser crash. I am truly pissed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T22:37:28-08:00","id":382757,"title":"","content":"Some of you are making the mistake of thinking that the power to wear someone's else face is primarily a Changing Moon thing.<br /> <br /> This ignores how useful the power is for Full Moons, who do not need to be social butterflies to use the faces of others to get close to their targets and kill them when their guards are down. It also ignores how useful the faces of others are for No Moons who want to infiltrate places of knowledge to learn, spy and steal. Both Full Moons and No Moons likewise find the disguises very useful for fleeing the scene of the crime.<br /> <br /> The power to take the faces of others is essentially <i>Lunar</i>, equally useful and important to all three Castes, and in fact to <i>any </i>possible Lunar Castes. There may be particular Lunar concepts that avoid the use of stolen human faces, but I cannot a Lunar Caste built upon an archetype that would not find disguises important.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, think about how powerful this ability would be. The power to assume someone's appearance at will, without a disguise action, without a Larceny roll, without Heart's Blood. Even if you lack the myriad benefits that could be derived from Heart's Blood (Attribute ratings, memories, Fate, attunements, Charms, etc.), just the ability to skip Heart's Blood as a requirement for taking someone's appearance is a huge advantage.<br /> <br /> It's an advantage you are suggesting that every Changing Moon should get for free, at character generation.<br /> <br /> Are you sure it doesn't make more sense as a Charm, which any Lunar can learn? Again, I remind you that disguise has far many more possible applications than exerting social influence!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:25:36-08:00","id":385050,"title":"","content":"Oh, forgot how the Changing Moon power would be utter hell in the hands of a Full Moon fighing against a party of opponents, not just for singular assassinations.<br /> <br /> Can you ever be sure you're trusting your back to your REAL friend in this hunt? Surprise backstab!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-02-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T10:54:48-08:00","id":390092,"title":"","content":"So, ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>* Add your Essence rating to your Charisma or Manipulation Attribute rating for the purpose of Intimidation actions</b><br /> useful when flaring or not, inside and outside of battle<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>* Add your Essence rating to your Manipulation rating for the purpose of preventing people from telling if you're lying</b><br /> useful when flaring or not (though more useful when not), inside and outside of battle (though generally more useful outside) -- works synergistically with the first power if you're trying to intimidate people with Manipulation, insofar as it makes it less likely for them to see through your bluff and render the Intimidation action pointless regardless of the bonus it received.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:56:59-08:00","id":423424,"title":"","content":"So, given Hatewheel's recent question (and conclusions) about how a &quot;look like anyone without Heart's Blood&quot; power would shake out for Lunars, I'm once again feeling confident in my own conclusions in this thread.<br /> <br /> Anyone else have any more thoughts for new Changing Moon anima affects actually related to being social power houses?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/414129-the-no-moon-is-the-trickster-and-the-changing-moon-is-the-shaman\">Especially given the idea that Changing Moons, rather than No Moons, are the better fit for the &quot;Shaman&quot; archetype?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}